3	// The subject of the printer panel's conversation: what the agent is told and
4	// may call there, what the panel pins above the thread, and what a tap on one
5	// of its cards does.
6	//
7	// A session is opened for one printer question -- add a printer, or change
8	// this one -- and is discarded when the panel closes. Nothing here is written
9	// to the project: AgentHost keeps the thread in an in-memory document, and
10	// the printers themselves are saved through IPrinterBackend, which owns the
11	// only route to Orca.
12	//
13	// GUI-free and Orca-free: the panel supplies both interfaces, and the tests
14	// supply fakes.
15	
